## Round Referee Note

**Slot 1 (run 36) won**, though all three candidates improved on their starting point (run 32). Slot 1 achieved setup_wns 0.0953 — essentially holding flat against the start's 0.0101 — while slot 2 actually gained slightly more absolute WNS (+0.0477) but closed less tightly. Slot 0 (UTIL 68) catastrophically failed: setup went to -0.026 with TNS -0.361, proving the design has no margin at 87% utilization.

**Key takeaway — the utilization cliff is steep and real.** Going from 62→66 costs only ~0.006 WNS (manageable), but 66→68 costs ~0.048 more — roughly an 8× acceleration in degradation. The curve is no longer linear; the design is running out of routing headroom above ~84% utilization. The CLOCK_PERIOD relaxation to 1.83 is helping across all three slots, but cannot rescue a severely overpacked design (slot 0 proves this).

**What to do next:** The current config (UTIL 66, CLOCK 1.83) is closed and solid. The most promising unexplored lever is **lowering CLOCK_PERIOD back slightly (say 1.80–1.82)** while holding UTIL at 66 — this tests whether we can recover a tighter clock now that we have a better utilization target. Separately, **SETUP_SLACK_MARGIN** at 0.025 or 0.05 (it has only been tested at 0.2 and 1.0) could tighten placement without the blunt force of high SLACK_MARGIN. The CORE_UTILIZATION knob should stop at 66 — going higher breaks timing, going lower wastes area. CELL_PAD_IN_SITES_GLOBAL_PLACEMENT at 1 showed a small positive effect earlier; testing it at 0 or 2 in combination with the current config is worth a slot.
